  },
  "scope_notes": "Changes validation interface notifications: same-txid different-witness transactions will now emit MemPoolRemovalReason::CONFLICT, sending an 'R' ZMQ sequence event and potentially triggering an extra unconfirmed wallet notification.",
  "changed_since_previous": "The PR now updates CTxMemPool::removeForBlock to check for exact wtxid matches, evicting witness-mismatched entries as conflicts instead of reporting them as mined block inclusions. Documentation and release notes were added detailing the resulting ZMQ sequence notifications and wallet effects.",
  "card": "Require an exact wtxid match before marking a mempool transaction as mined during block connection, removing same-txid witness variants as conflicts instead. Previously, removeForBlock matched only by txid, allowing unmined witness variants to count as confirmed, skewing mempool fee estimator health calculations and misinforming fee tracking, wallet notifications, and ZMQ subscribers. In addition to emitting conflict notifications for mismatched witnesses, the mempool estimator now evaluates coverage using mined block transaction weights directly.",
